# Write effective links

<h2 id="wg-083">Describe the destination in the link text</h2>

The link text must make sense on its own. Do not use “click here”, “more” or a bare URL. A link goes somewhere. It does not run a device action.

<%= example('wg-accessible-links') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| For help, click here. | Read how to [reset the hallway motion sensor](#). |
| More | [Open the Zigbee router guide](#) |
| Turn off the heating (a link that switches it off) | Select the **Turn off heating** button. |

Put each link in the sentence where it is useful. Do not collect them at the bottom.

<h2 id="wg-037">Say when a link leaves Home Assistant</h2>

Name external services, downloads and new tabs before the person selects. Do not put personal data, passwords or tokens in a link.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| More | [Open the manufacturer’s support page (opens another website)](#) |
| Download | [Download the diagnostics file (.json, 140KB)](#) |
| https://example.com/reset?user=nain&token=abc123 | [Reset your password on the manufacturer’s website](#) |

Link to the specific page, not a homepage. Do not link to a service that needs an account to read the answer unless the task needs it. Do not claim an external page works without the internet.
